1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:04,500
Every tenth of November, the oldest Marine
in the room hands a piece of cake to

2
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:05,820
the youngest.

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:11,174
It started here, in 1775:
two battalions of Marines.

4
00:00:11,364 --> 00:00:13,874
Every generation since
has added to the line.

5
00:00:13,924 --> 00:00:17,144
Tripoli. Belleau Wood.
Iwo Jima. Chosin. Huế.

6
00:00:17,194 --> 00:00:18,289
Fallujah.

7
00:00:20,374 --> 00:00:26,484
In 1921, Commandant Lejeune ordered
a message read on every birthday.

8
00:00:26,534 --> 00:00:31,194
It still is: 'This high name we have
received from those who preceded us.'

9
00:00:31,414 --> 00:00:36,084
That's what the cake is.
Nobody earns the title alone.

10
00:00:36,134 --> 00:00:38,394
Keep faith with the Marines
who came before you,

11
00:00:38,444 --> 00:00:40,022
and hand it on.

12
00:00:40,232 --> 00:00:44,275
Semper Fidelis. Happy birthday, Marines.
